                <pb facs="0318" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-28T18:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your 54, August 27, 5 p.m. The Department is of the opinion that no issue of
                    recognition need arise. You should therefore continue normal relations with the
                    Bolivian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
